Relevant tables / columns and their potential usage  
• SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "path": locate files whose path ends with ‘README.md’  
  – "id": join key that links the file‑record with its blob/content record  
  – "repo_name": repository the README belongs to  
  – "ref": branch/tag (not essential here, but could scope to a particular ref)  

• SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "id": join key coming from SAMPLE_FILES."id"  
  – "content": complete text of the file to be split into lines  
  – "sample_repo_name": duplicate of repository name (either this or SAMPLE_FILES."repo_name" may be used)  
  – "binary": filter out binaries (should be FALSE)  
  – "size": could be used to ignore empty files (>0)  

• LANGUAGES  
  – "repo_name": key to join with repository name from FILES / CONTENTS  
  – "language": list/array (stored as variant text) of programming languages; will be aggregated per line  

Typical conditions that will be useful  
1. "path" ILIKE '%README.md' – restrict to README files (case‑insensitive)  
2. "binary" = FALSE – exclude binary blobs  
3. "content" IS NOT NULL AND "size" > 0 – keep only valid readable files  
4. Split "content" on line breaks, then  
     TRIM("line") <> ''                      – non‑empty lines  
     NOT TRIM("line") ILIKE '#%'             – ignore Markdown comments beginning with #  
     NOT TRIM("line") ILIKE '//%'            – ignore code‑style line comments  
5. GROUP BY normalised line, COUNT(DISTINCT repo_name) – frequency of each unique line  
6. LISTAGG(DISTINCT language, ',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY language) – comma‑separated list of languages, alphabetical  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (all limited to 20 rows) that move from simple inspection toward the final composite query.  
Every column and identifier is enclosed in double quotes per requirement.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Quick look at any README.md file names that exist.
SELECT DISTINCT "repo_name",
       "path"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  "path" ILIKE '%README.md'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Show README blobs (id + size) that are NOT binary.
SELECT sf."id",
       sf."repo_name",
       sc."size",
       sc."binary"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES   sf
JOIN   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
       ON sf."id" = sc."id"
WHERE  sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
  AND  sc."binary" = FALSE
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Peek at the first few characters of README content.
SELECT sf."repo_name",
       LEFT(sc."content", 120) AS "snippet"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES   sf
JOIN   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
       ON sf."id" = sc."id"
WHERE  sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
  AND  sc."binary" = FALSE
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Explode one README into individual lines.
SELECT sf."repo_name",
       lt.value::STRING AS "line"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES   sf
JOIN   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
       ON sf."id" = sc."id",
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(sc."content", '\n')) lt
WHERE  sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
  AND  sc."binary" = FALSE
  AND  sf."repo_name" = (SELECT MIN("repo_name")
                         FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
                         WHERE "path" ILIKE '%README.md')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Keep only non‑empty, non‑comment lines from READMEs.
SELECT lt.value::STRING AS "clean_line"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES   sf
JOIN   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
       ON sf."id" = sc."id",
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(sc."content", '\n')) lt
WHERE  sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
  AND  sc."binary" = FALSE
  AND  TRIM(lt.value::STRING) <> ''
  AND  NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '#%'
  AND  NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '//%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Frequency of each unique README line (across repos).
SELECT   TRIM(lt.value::STRING)               AS "line",
         COUNT(DISTINCT sf."repo_name")       AS "repo_count"
FROM     GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES   sf
JOIN     GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
         ON sf."id" = sc."id",
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(sc."content", '\n')) lt
WHERE    sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
  AND    sc."binary" = FALSE
  AND    TRIM(lt.value::STRING) <> ''
  AND    NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '#%'
  AND    NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '//%'
GROUP BY TRIM(lt.value::STRING)
ORDER BY "repo_count" DESC
LIMIT    20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Link repositories to their language lists.
SELECT   "repo_name",
         "language"
FROM     GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES
LIMIT    20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Attach languages to each non‑comment README line for one repo.
SELECT   sf."repo_name",
         TRIM(lt.value::STRING)                 AS "line",
         lg."language"
FROM     GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES     sf
JOIN     GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  sc
         ON sf."id" = sc."id",
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(sc."content", '\n')) lt
LEFT JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES        lg
         ON lg."repo_name" = sf."repo_name"
WHERE    sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
  AND    sc."binary" = FALSE
  AND    TRIM(lt.value::STRING) <> ''
  AND    NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '#%'
  AND    NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '//%'
  AND    sf."repo_name" = (SELECT MIN("repo_name")
                           FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
                           WHERE "path" ILIKE '%README.md')
LIMIT    20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Build comma‑separated language list per unique line
--                 (only counting repositories where the line appears).
SELECT   line_details."line",
         COUNT(DISTINCT line_details."repo_name")                           AS "frequency",
         LISTAGG(DISTINCT lg."language", ',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY lg."language") AS "languages"
FROM   (
         SELECT DISTINCT
                sf."repo_name",
                TRIM(lt.value::STRING) AS "line"
         FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES    sf
         JOIN   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
                ON sf."id" = sc."id",
                LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(sc."content", '\n')) lt
         WHERE  sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
           AND  sc."binary" = FALSE
           AND  TRIM(lt.value::STRING) <> ''
           AND  NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '#%'
           AND  NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '//%'
       ) line_details
LEFT JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES lg
       ON lg."repo_name" = line_details."repo_name"
GROUP BY line_details."line"
ORDER BY "frequency" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Same as query 9 but restrict to lines that mention 'install'.
SELECT   line_details."line",
         COUNT(DISTINCT line_details."repo_name")                           AS "frequency",
         LISTAGG(DISTINCT lg."language", ',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY lg."language") AS "languages"
FROM   (
         SELECT DISTINCT
                sf."repo_name",
                TRIM(lt.value::STRING) AS "line"
         FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES    sf
         JOIN   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS sc
                ON sf."id" = sc."id",
                LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(sc."content", '\n')) lt
         WHERE  sf."path" ILIKE '%README.md'
           AND  sc."binary" = FALSE
           AND  TRIM(lt.value::STRING) <> ''
           AND  NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '#%'
           AND  NOT TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '//%'
           AND  TRIM(lt.value::STRING) ILIKE '%install%'
       ) line_details
LEFT JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES lg
       ON lg."repo_name" = line_details."repo_name"
GROUP BY line_details."line"
ORDER BY "frequency" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
